1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:20,000
BrandPilot Local turns one product image and campaign brief into reviewable, platform-ready marketing concepts.

2
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:50,000
It joins asset intake, audience and benefits, brand direction, formats, copy, and approval in one responsive local workspace.

3
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Mock mode is the default. This local demonstration needs no GPU, model weights, or external service.

4
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:50,000
The product brief creates four clearly labelled mock campaign directions. These demonstrate the workflow, not Radeon output.

5
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Copy and review state can be changed, and the Approved decision persists after refresh.

6
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Experimental Radeon mode is a temporary authenticated opt-in with one GPU job, lazy loading, and no CPU or mock fallback.

7
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:55,000
The real image shown here was generated on AMD Radeon with ROCm during our verified cloud session.

8
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:15,000
The pinned SDXL run used 768 by 768 output, 15 steps, strength 0.35, guidance 6.5, and seed 20260725.

9
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Cold load measured 132.295 seconds and generation 222.111 seconds, with measured peak GPU memory recorded in the repository.

10
00:03:30,000 --> 00:04:00,000
The official public browser edge remained blocked because its assigned hostname did not resolve in public DNS. No success was fabricated, and every instance was destroyed.

11
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:30,000
BrandPilot's value is the accountable system around generation: brand context, multiple directions, formats, provenance, and human review.

12
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:40,000
BrandPilot Local was created by Talal Khawaja and Aqeela Urooj for Track 1. Thank you.
